When a prompt is sent to GPT, it is first tokenized into Token IDs. The embedding layer converts those IDs into dense vectors, and positional
information is added so the model understands token order. The Transformer layers use self-attention and feed-forward networks to build contextual representations.
The output layer computes scores for every token in the vocabulary, softmax converts those scores into probabilities, and the model selects the next Token ID. Finally,
the tokenizer decodes that Token ID into readable text. This process repeats one token at a time until the entire response is generated.


